window.CPY701 = {"course": "CPY 701 \u00b7 Introduction to Counseling Psychology", "programme": "Master's Degree in Counseling Psychology", "weeks": [{"id": "w01", "num": 1, "title": "The Nature and Concept of Counseling Psychology", "slides": [{"file": "/dist/slides/w01/01-title.png", "title": "Introduction to Counseling Psychology", "start": 0.0, "end": 30.59}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/02-outcomes.png", "title": "What you will be able to do by the end of this week", "start": 30.59, "end": 66.84}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/03-working-picture.png", "title": "Counseling psychology: a working picture", "start": 66.84, "end": 115.46}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/04-definitions.png", "title": "Three definitions worth keeping", "start": 115.46, "end": 166.78}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/05-rogers.png", "title": "rogers", "start": 166.78, "end": 191.45}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/06-helping-continuum.png", "title": "The helping continuum", "start": 191.45, "end": 241.18}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/07-compare-three.png", "title": "Guidance, counseling and psychotherapy side by side", "start": 241.18, "end": 286.58}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/08-neighbours.png", "title": "Counseling psychology among its neighbours", "start": 286.58, "end": 336.84}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/09-core-values.png", "title": "Six values that give the specialty its character", "start": 336.84, "end": 379.14}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/10-scope.png", "title": "What counseling psychologists actually do", "start": 379.14, "end": 423.88}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/11-limits.png", "title": "Where competence ends and referral begins", "start": 423.88, "end": 470.79}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/12-spa-model.png", "title": "The scientist-practitioner-advocate identity", "start": 470.79, "end": 514.21}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/13-art-science.png", "title": "Counseling as science and as art", "start": 514.21, "end": 552.57}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/14-person-of-counselor.png", "title": "The person of the counselor", "start": 552.57, "end": 594.74}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/15-summary.png", "title": "Week 1 in review", "start": 594.74, "end": 632.63}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/16-task.png", "title": "Applied task and next week", "start": 632.63, "end": 674.87}], "cues": [{"s": 0.0, "e": 5.85, "t": "Welcome to CPY 701, Introduction to Counseling Psychology, a core course in the Master's"}, {"s": 5.85, "e": 11.51, "t": "degree in Counseling Psychology. I am glad you are here. This is week one of sixteen,"}, {"s": 11.51, "e": 17.22, "t": "and in this first lecture we ask the most fundamental question of all: what exactly is"}, {"s": 17.22, "e": 22.55, "t": "counseling psychology? By the end of this session you will be able to define the"}, {"s": 22.55, "e": 28.33, "t": "specialty, place it on the helping continuum, and describe the values, scope and limits"}, {"s": 28.33, "e": 30.59, "t": "that govern professional practice."}, {"s": 30.59, "e": 36.05, "t": "Here is what this week promises. First, you will define counseling psychology from"}, {"s": 36.05, "e": 41.1, "t": "authoritative sources. Second, you will distinguish guidance, counseling and"}, {"s": 41.1, "e": 46.69, "t": "psychotherapy without confusing them. Third, you will explain the core values of the"}, {"s": 46.69, "e": 52.41, "t": "specialty and its scope of practice, including where your competence ends and referral"}, {"s": 52.41, "e": 58.2, "t": "begins. And fourth, you will describe the scientist, practitioner and advocate identity"}, {"s": 58.2, "e": 63.98, "t": "that this programme expects you to grow into. Keep these four outcomes beside you as we"}, {"s": 63.98, "e": 66.84, "t": "move; every slide today serves one of them."}, {"s": 66.84, "e": 72.56, "t": "Let us begin with a working picture. Counseling psychology is a professional specialty"}, {"s": 72.56, "e": 78.02, "t": "within psychology. It applies psychological theory, research and technique to help"}, {"s": 78.02, "e": 83.54, "t": "people improve their wellbeing, resolve problems in living, and develop personally,"}, {"s": 83.54, "e": 89.19, "t": "socially, educationally and vocationally. Notice three things in that sentence. It is"}, {"s": 89.19, "e": 95.04, "t": "professional: it is governed by training, ethics and regulation, not by good intentions."}, {"s": 95.04, "e": 100.83, "t": "It is psychological: it works through mental processes, behaviour and relationship, not"}, {"s": 100.83, "e": 106.61, "t": "through medicine or coercion. And it is helping: its engine is a deliberate, boundaried"}, {"s": 106.61, "e": 112.4, "t": "relationship between a trained counselor and a client who seeks change. Everything else"}, {"s": 112.4, "e": 115.46, "t": "in this course grows from those three anchors."}, {"s": 115.46, "e": 121.05, "t": "Now let three authoritative voices sharpen the definition. The Society of Counseling"}, {"s": 121.05, "e": 126.78, "t": "Psychology, Division 17 of the American Psychological Association, describes the field"}, {"s": 126.78, "e": 132.17, "t": "as a specialty that facilitates personal and interpersonal functioning across the"}, {"s": 132.17, "e": 137.76, "t": "lifespan, focusing on emotional, social, vocational, educational, health-related and"}, {"s": 137.76, "e": 143.28, "t": "developmental concerns. Corey reminds us that counseling is a collaborative process"}, {"s": 143.28, "e": 148.67, "t": "between two people, in which the counselor's attitudes and skills help the client"}, {"s": 148.67, "e": 154.26, "t": "examine and change behaviour. Gladding calls counseling the professional practice of"}, {"s": 154.26, "e": 160.12, "t": "helping people who are not severely disturbed to solve problems and make decisions. Hear"}, {"s": 160.12, "e": 165.98, "t": "the common thread: ordinary people, real problems, a trained helper, and change that the"}, {"s": 165.98, "e": 166.78, "t": "client owns."}, {"s": 166.78, "e": 172.5, "t": "Carl Rogers left us a line that captures the heart of our work: the curious paradox is"}, {"s": 172.5, "e": 178.28, "t": "that when I accept myself just as I am, then I can change. Counseling psychology is not"}, {"s": 178.28, "e": 184.07, "t": "about fixing broken people. It is about creating conditions in which a person, accepted"}, {"s": 184.07, "e": 189.78, "t": "and understood, can move toward their own potential. Hold that paradox; it will return"}, {"s": 189.78, "e": 191.45, "t": "in every theory we study."}, {"s": 191.45, "e": 196.83, "t": "Where does counseling sit on the helping road? Picture a continuum. At one end is"}, {"s": 196.83, "e": 202.62, "t": "guidance: informative, preventive and often educational, giving students or clients the"}, {"s": 202.62, "e": 208.4, "t": "information and direction they need, for example choosing a course or a career. Next is"}, {"s": 208.4, "e": 214.12, "t": "counseling: a deeper, relational process with clients who are experiencing adjustment,"}, {"s": 214.12, "e": 219.24, "t": "developmental or situational distress but remain within the range of ordinary"}, {"s": 219.24, "e": 224.36, "t": "functioning. Further along is psychotherapy: longer, more intensive work with"}, {"s": 224.36, "e": 229.95, "t": "deeper-seated personality or chronic emotional difficulties. And at the far end sits"}, {"s": 229.95, "e": 235.67, "t": "psychiatric and medical treatment, where diagnosis and medication lead. The boundaries"}, {"s": 235.67, "e": 241.18, "t": "blur in practice, but the direction of travel, depth, duration and training differ."}, {"s": 241.18, "e": 246.9, "t": "Let us make those differences concrete. Guidance is typically brief, informational and"}, {"s": 246.9, "e": 252.68, "t": "preventive; its client is often a student or a group; a teacher or guidance officer may"}, {"s": 252.68, "e": 258.2, "t": "deliver it. Counseling is relational and focused on present problems in living; its"}, {"s": 258.2, "e": 263.91, "t": "client is a person or couple in situational distress; the counselor holds postgraduate"}, {"s": 263.91, "e": 269.56, "t": "professional training. Psychotherapy runs longer, works with more entrenched patterns"}, {"s": 269.56, "e": 275.28, "t": "and often with diagnosed disorders; the psychotherapist or clinical psychologist leads"}, {"s": 275.28, "e": 280.93, "t": "it. Memorise the table's dimensions, focus, client, duration, depth and practitioner,"}, {"s": 280.93, "e": 286.58, "t": "because examination questions love to ask you to distinguish these three in practice."}, {"s": 286.58, "e": 292.23, "t": "A frequent confusion: how is counseling psychology different from clinical psychology"}, {"s": 292.23, "e": 297.48, "t": "and psychiatry? We share much: assessment, diagnostic awareness, evidence-based"}, {"s": 297.48, "e": 302.93, "t": "intervention, and ethics. What distinguishes us is emphasis. Counseling psychology"}, {"s": 302.93, "e": 308.59, "t": "stresses strengths and resources, not only pathology; it works with developmental and"}, {"s": 308.59, "e": 314.3, "t": "vocational concerns as seriously as with disorder; it favours brief, focal, preventive"}, {"s": 314.3, "e": 320.02, "t": "intervention; and it treats culture, context and social justice as clinical facts, not"}, {"s": 320.02, "e": 325.74, "t": "footnotes. Psychiatry adds medical training and prescribing; clinical psychology leans"}, {"s": 325.74, "e": 331.52, "t": "harder on severe psychopathology and assessment batteries. Knowing the overlap protects"}, {"s": 331.52, "e": 336.84, "t": "you from turf wars; knowing the distinction protects your professional identity."}, {"s": 336.84, "e": 342.5, "t": "Six values give the specialty its character. Wellness and prevention: we would rather"}, {"s": 342.5, "e": 348.15, "t": "strengthen a community than only repair damage. Strengths and resilience: we hunt for"}, {"s": 348.15, "e": 353.8, "t": "resources, not merely deficits. Development across the lifespan: a twelve-year-old, a"}, {"s": 353.8, "e": 359.59, "t": "forty-year-old and a seventy-year-old face different tasks, and we meet each where they"}, {"s": 359.59, "e": 365.18, "t": "are. Multicultural and social justice commitment: culture, faith, gender and poverty"}, {"s": 365.18, "e": 370.76, "t": "shape distress and help-seeking. Brief, focal, evidence-informed practice: we choose"}, {"s": 370.76, "e": 376.42, "t": "what works, and we measure it. And advocacy: sometimes the most therapeutic act is to"}, {"s": 376.42, "e": 379.14, "t": "change the system that wounds the client."}, {"s": 379.14, "e": 384.4, "t": "What does the scope of practice look like on the ground? Populations: children,"}, {"s": 384.4, "e": 390.26, "t": "adolescents, students, couples, families, workers and older adults. Concerns: adjustment"}, {"s": 390.26, "e": 396.05, "t": "to change, academic and examination stress, career decision-making, grief, relationship"}, {"s": 396.05, "e": 401.58, "t": "conflict, mild to moderate anxiety and depression, trauma reactions, health-related"}, {"s": 401.58, "e": 406.84, "t": "adjustment, and substance-use concerns at an early stage. Settings: schools and"}, {"s": 406.84, "e": 412.36, "t": "universities, hospitals and clinics, workplaces and employee assistance programmes,"}, {"s": 412.36, "e": 417.36, "t": "rehabilitation centres, faith and community organisations, non-governmental"}, {"s": 417.36, "e": 423.22, "t": "organisations, and private or telepractice. Wide, yes. Unlimited, no. And that brings us"}, {"s": 423.22, "e": 423.88, "t": "to limits."}, {"s": 423.88, "e": 429.2, "t": "Competence has edges, and naming them is a professional act, not a confession of"}, {"s": 429.2, "e": 434.93, "t": "weakness. Refer onward when you meet psychosis or severe mood disorder with risk; when"}, {"s": 434.93, "e": 440.58, "t": "medical causes may explain the presentation; when the client needs medication review;"}, {"s": 440.58, "e": 446.3, "t": "when forensic or custody questions arise; when the problem exceeds your training, such"}, {"s": 446.3, "e": 451.96, "t": "as specialist eating-disorder or addiction treatment; and whenever your own values or"}, {"s": 451.96, "e": 457.42, "t": "relationship with the client compromise objectivity. Equally, refer in: counseling"}, {"s": 457.42, "e": 463.27, "t": "psychologists work inside multidisciplinary teams, and a warm referral letter is part of"}, {"s": 463.27, "e": 468.93, "t": "the intervention. If you ever feel unsure whether a case is yours, supervision exists"}, {"s": 468.93, "e": 470.79, "t": "precisely for that question."}, {"s": 470.79, "e": 476.31, "t": "So who are you becoming? The classic answer is the scientist, practitioner, and, in"}, {"s": 476.31, "e": 481.89, "t": "newer formulations, the advocate. As scientist you consume and produce evidence: you"}, {"s": 481.89, "e": 487.48, "t": "read outcome research, you measure your own results, you stay humble before data. As"}, {"s": 487.48, "e": 493.33, "t": "practitioner you translate that evidence into skilful, timely, humane action with a real"}, {"s": 493.33, "e": 498.98, "t": "person in front of you. As advocate you notice that some suffering is manufactured by"}, {"s": 498.98, "e": 504.83, "t": "unjust systems, and you act to change conditions, in schools, workplaces and policy. The"}, {"s": 504.83, "e": 510.69, "t": "gold centre of this triangle is you: the integrated counseling psychologist, holding all"}, {"s": 510.69, "e": 514.21, "t": "three roles without letting any one of them dominate."}, {"s": 514.21, "e": 519.53, "t": "Is counseling an art or a science? The honest answer is both, and the tension is"}, {"s": 519.53, "e": 524.85, "t": "creative. The science side gives you theory, technique, measurement and research"}, {"s": 524.85, "e": 530.56, "t": "evidence: what to do, in what order, with what expected effect. The art side gives you"}, {"s": 530.56, "e": 536.35, "t": "timing, presence, language and intuition: knowing when to be silent, when to challenge,"}, {"s": 536.35, "e": 541.8, "t": "when a metaphor will land where a lecture would bounce off. Science without art is"}, {"s": 541.8, "e": 547.51, "t": "mechanical and cold; art without science is charming but unaccountable. Our discipline"}, {"s": 547.51, "e": 552.57, "t": "asks you to be rigorous enough to be trusted and human enough to be helpful."}, {"s": 552.57, "e": 558.22, "t": "Finally this week, a preview of the person of the counselor. Technical skill will not"}, {"s": 558.22, "e": 564.01, "t": "carry you if the person behind the skill is unexamined. The qualities we will cultivate"}, {"s": 564.01, "e": 569.79, "t": "across this programme include self-awareness and honesty about your own wounds; warmth,"}, {"s": 569.79, "e": 575.65, "t": "respect and genuineness; emotional stability and the capacity to tolerate another's pain"}, {"s": 575.65, "e": 580.97, "t": "without collapsing or fleeing; openness to culture and difference; courage to be"}, {"s": 580.97, "e": 586.42, "t": "challenged and to change; and a disciplined ethical conscience. Start a reflective"}, {"s": 586.42, "e": 592.14, "t": "journal now, this week. One page after every skills practice. By week fifteen you will"}, {"s": 592.14, "e": 594.74, "t": "see a counselor forming in those pages."}, {"s": 594.74, "e": 600.25, "t": "Let us gather the week. Counseling psychology applies psychological science to help"}, {"s": 600.25, "e": 605.97, "t": "people improve functioning and wellbeing across the lifespan. It sits between guidance"}, {"s": 605.97, "e": 611.76, "t": "and psychotherapy on the helping continuum, distinguished by focus, depth, duration and"}, {"s": 611.76, "e": 617.61, "t": "training. It shares ground with clinical psychology and psychiatry while keeping its own"}, {"s": 617.61, "e": 623.06, "t": "emphasis on strengths, development, prevention and culture. Its scope is broad but"}, {"s": 623.06, "e": 628.71, "t": "bounded, and referral is a skill, not a failure. And it is lived through a scientist,"}, {"s": 628.71, "e": 632.63, "t": "practitioner, advocate identity held by an examined person."}, {"s": 632.63, "e": 637.82, "t": "Your task before next week. Write your own sixty-word definition of counseling"}, {"s": 637.82, "e": 643.34, "t": "psychology, then defend it in one paragraph against the strongest objection you can"}, {"s": 643.34, "e": 648.79, "t": "imagine. Second, observe one helping conversation in your community, a teacher and"}, {"s": 648.79, "e": 654.45, "t": "student, a pastor and a member, a friend and a friend, and note which helping mode it"}, {"s": 654.45, "e": 660.1, "t": "was: guidance, counseling, or something else. Bring both to the seminar. Next week we"}, {"s": 660.1, "e": 665.89, "t": "travel through history, from Frank Parsons to the first graduate training in counseling"}, {"s": 665.89, "e": 671.74, "t": "psychology in Nigeria. Read Corey and Gladding's history chapters before then. Thank you"}, {"s": 671.74, "e": 674.87, "t": "for your attention; I will see you in week two."}], "mode": "captions", "duration": 674.87}, {"id": "w02", "num": 2, "title": "Historical and Philosophical Development", "slides": [{"file": "/dist/slides/w02/01-title.png", "title": "Historical and Philosophical Development", "start": 0.0, "end": 32.04}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/02-outcomes.png", "title": "What you will be able to do by the end of this week", "start": 32.04, "end": 64.93}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/03-why-history.png", "title": "Why a whole week on history?", "start": 64.93, "end": 104.08}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/04-timeline-1.png", "title": "How the specialty was seeded", "start": 104.08, "end": 153.75}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/05-timeline-2.png", "title": "How the specialty grew up", "start": 153.75, "end": 202.04}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/06-figures.png", "title": "The ancestors, briefly", "start": 202.04, "end": 251.38}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/07-great-debate.png", "title": "Rogers versus Williamson: the debate that built our habits", "start": 251.38, "end": 294.87}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/08-parsons-quote.png", "title": "parsons-quote", "start": 294.87, "end": 325.13}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/09-indigenous-helping.png", "title": "Indigenous and faith-based helping systems", "start": 325.13, "end": 375.2}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/10-nigeria-formal.png", "title": "Counseling psychology in Nigeria: five movements", "start": 375.2, "end": 422.76}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/11-two-histories.png", "title": "Two histories, one profession", "start": 422.76, "end": 473.62}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/12-assumptions.png", "title": "The assumptions underneath the history", "start": 473.62, "end": 519.61}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/13-six-isms.png", "title": "Six commitments that decode every theory", "start": 519.61, "end": 557.24}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/14-obligations.png", "title": "What history obligates you to do", "start": 557.24, "end": 593.36}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/15-summary.png", "title": "Week 2 in review", "start": 593.36, "end": 633.62}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/16-task.png", "title": "Applied task and next week", "start": 633.62, "end": 672.76}], "cues": [{"s": 0.0, "e": 5.52, "t": "Welcome back to CPY 701. Week one gave us a definition; week two gives us a memory."}, {"s": 5.52, "e": 11.1, "t": "Today we trace how counseling psychology came to be, from Frank Parsons's vocational"}, {"s": 11.1, "e": 16.62, "t": "bureau in Boston in 1908, through the mental hygiene movement and the wars, to Carl"}, {"s": 16.62, "e": 21.94, "t": "Rogers's quiet revolution, and then home: to Nigeria, where graduate training in"}, {"s": 21.94, "e": 27.79, "t": "counseling psychology began at the University of Nigeria, Nsukka in 1994. History is not"}, {"s": 27.79, "e": 32.04, "t": "decoration in this course; it explains why we practice as we do."}, {"s": 32.04, "e": 37.56, "t": "Four outcomes for this week. One, construct a timeline of the field from vocational"}, {"s": 37.56, "e": 43.34, "t": "guidance to the present. Two, identify the contribution of key figures: Parsons, Beers,"}, {"s": 43.34, "e": 48.85, "t": "Rogers, Williamson and Super. Three, explain how counseling psychology developed in"}, {"s": 48.85, "e": 54.24, "t": "Nigeria and Africa, including regulation and the Mental Health Act of 2022. Four,"}, {"s": 54.24, "e": 59.88, "t": "articulate the philosophical assumptions, humanistic, phenomenological, developmental"}, {"s": 59.88, "e": 64.93, "t": "and contextual, that undergird our practice. Keep them in view as we travel."}, {"s": 64.93, "e": 70.58, "t": "Why spend a whole week on history at master's level? Because every technique you will"}, {"s": 70.58, "e": 76.3, "t": "learn carries an argument inside it. When you reflect feeling, you are taking Rogers's"}, {"s": 76.3, "e": 81.68, "t": "side in a debate that began in the 1940s. When you screen a client, you inherit a"}, {"s": 81.68, "e": 87.33, "t": "psychometric tradition born in army camps in 1917. When you advocate for a community,"}, {"s": 87.33, "e": 92.71, "t": "you continue the prevention movement of the 1960s. History tells you what you are"}, {"s": 92.71, "e": 98.43, "t": "standing on, so that you can stand deliberately rather than by habit. It also protects"}, {"s": 98.43, "e": 104.08, "t": "you from chronological snobbery: old does not mean false, and new does not mean true."}, {"s": 104.08, "e": 109.53, "t": "Begin at the beginning. 1908, Boston: Frank Parsons opens the Vocations Bureau and"}, {"s": 109.53, "e": 115.18, "t": "proposes that wise career choice rests on self-knowledge, occupational knowledge, and"}, {"s": 115.18, "e": 120.77, "t": "true reasoning between them, the seed of trait-and-factor counseling. The same year,"}, {"s": 120.77, "e": 126.09, "t": "Clifford Beers turns his own asylum experience into the mental hygiene movement,"}, {"s": 126.09, "e": 131.28, "t": "planting prevention and humane reform. 1917 to 1918: the First World War makes"}, {"s": 131.28, "e": 136.46, "t": "psychological testing industrial-scale with the Army Alpha and Beta batteries;"}, {"s": 136.46, "e": 142.31, "t": "assessment enters public life. 1942: Carl Rogers publishes Counseling and Psychotherapy,"}, {"s": 142.31, "e": 148.16, "t": "and the client, not the diagnosis, moves to the centre. 1946: the American Psychological"}, {"s": 148.16, "e": 153.75, "t": "Association charts Division 17, and counseling psychology becomes a named specialty."}, {"s": 153.75, "e": 159.47, "t": "The second half of the century professionalizes the specialty. From 1949 and 1951, the"}, {"s": 159.47, "e": 165.12, "t": "Boulder conference's scientist-practitioner model and Veterans Administration funding"}, {"s": 165.12, "e": 170.84, "t": "shape graduate training: the counselor as both researcher and clinician. The community"}, {"s": 170.84, "e": 176.03, "t": "mental health movement of the 1960s pushes practice out of the clinic and into"}, {"s": 176.03, "e": 181.42, "t": "communities, strengthening prevention and outreach. The 1970s and 1980s bring the"}, {"s": 181.42, "e": 186.87, "t": "developmental turn: lifespan growth, wellness and vocational development become as"}, {"s": 186.87, "e": 192.73, "t": "central as remediation. Then the multicultural turn of the 1980s and 1990s makes culture"}, {"s": 192.73, "e": 198.25, "t": "and social justice clinical necessities. And our own century adds outcome research,"}, {"s": 198.25, "e": 202.04, "t": "measurement-based care, teletherapy and digital practice."}, {"s": 202.04, "e": 207.63, "t": "Meet the ancestors briefly. Frank Parsons, engineer and reformer, gave us vocational"}, {"s": 207.63, "e": 213.21, "t": "matching and the very idea of systematic guidance. Clifford Beers, a former patient,"}, {"s": 213.21, "e": 218.4, "t": "gave us the moral impulse: humane care and prevention. Carl Rogers gave us the"}, {"s": 218.4, "e": 223.78, "t": "relationship: empathy, congruence and unconditional positive regard as measurable"}, {"s": 223.78, "e": 229.37, "t": "conditions of change. Edward G. Williamson, at Minnesota, defended a more directive,"}, {"s": 229.37, "e": 234.69, "t": "structured trait-and-factor approach, and the Rogers-Williamson debate trained a"}, {"s": 234.69, "e": 240.21, "t": "generation to think about method. Donald Super gave career development its lifespan"}, {"s": 240.21, "e": 245.93, "t": "psychology. And in Nigeria, the pioneers who opened postgraduate training at Nsukka in"}, {"s": 245.93, "e": 251.38, "t": "1994 gave our own context its first cohort of home-grown counseling psychologists."}, {"s": 251.38, "e": 256.77, "t": "That Rogers-Williamson debate deserves a slide of its own, because it created our"}, {"s": 256.77, "e": 262.49, "t": "professional habit of arguing with evidence. Williamson's Minnesota point of view held"}, {"s": 262.49, "e": 267.94, "t": "that clients benefit from structured, directive guidance: assessment, information,"}, {"s": 267.94, "e": 273.79, "t": "advice where warranted. Rogers held that the client carries the capacity for change, and"}, {"s": 273.79, "e": 279.51, "t": "the counselor's job is to provide conditions, not directions. The field did not simply"}, {"s": 279.51, "e": 284.89, "t": "pick a side; it learned to test. From that quarrel came outcome research, process"}, {"s": 284.89, "e": 290.61, "t": "research, and the scientist-practitioner compact that still governs us: research feeds"}, {"s": 290.61, "e": 294.87, "t": "practice, and practice poses the questions research must answer."}, {"s": 294.87, "e": 300.52, "t": "Parsons left us the cleanest statement of the early vision, and it still reads like a"}, {"s": 300.52, "e": 306.31, "t": "counseling contract: three factors enter into wise career choice, a clear understanding"}, {"s": 306.31, "e": 311.83, "t": "of yourself, a knowledge of the requirements and conditions of success in different"}, {"s": 311.83, "e": 317.62, "t": "occupations, and true reasoning about the relations of these two groups of facts. Self,"}, {"s": 317.62, "e": 323.4, "t": "context, and disciplined reflection between them: that is counseling in one sentence, a"}, {"s": 323.4, "e": 325.13, "t": "century before our jargon."}, {"s": 325.13, "e": 330.66, "t": "Now bring the story home. Long before any bureau or clinic, African communities ran"}, {"s": 330.66, "e": 336.45, "t": "sophisticated helping systems. The extended family and its elders mediated conflict and"}, {"s": 336.45, "e": 342.04, "t": "guided the young; age grades and titles carried mentorship duties; religious leaders"}, {"s": 342.04, "e": 347.5, "t": "offered counsel and meaning; traditional healers addressed distress in an idiom of"}, {"s": 347.5, "e": 352.89, "t": "spirit, ancestor and community. Communal philosophies, ubuntu in the south of the"}, {"s": 352.89, "e": 358.09, "t": "continent, omoluwabi and similar ethics in Yoruba land, framed the person as a"}, {"s": 358.09, "e": 363.75, "t": "person-through-others. These systems supplied continuity, meaning and accountability."}, {"s": 363.75, "e": 369.01, "t": "They also carried limits we must name: stigma around mental distress, spiritual"}, {"s": 369.01, "e": 374.86, "t": "attribution that could delay medical care, and confidentiality norms very different from"}, {"s": 374.86, "e": 375.2, "t": "ours."}, {"s": 375.2, "e": 381.05, "t": "Formal counseling psychology in Nigeria arrives in five movements. In the 1950s and 60s,"}, {"s": 381.05, "e": 386.91, "t": "post-independence school expansion creates guidance services and the teacher-counsellor."}, {"s": 386.91, "e": 392.49, "t": "Through the 1970s and 80s, universities establish guidance and counselling units and"}, {"s": 392.49, "e": 397.68, "t": "departments, and professional associations form to set standards. In 1994, the"}, {"s": 397.68, "e": 403.54, "t": "University of Nigeria, Nsukka begins postgraduate training in counseling psychology, the"}, {"s": 403.54, "e": 408.79, "t": "moment our specialty acquires a graduate pipeline of its own. In the 2000s, the"}, {"s": 408.79, "e": 414.65, "t": "Counsellors Registration Council of Nigeria brings statutory registration and standards."}, {"s": 414.65, "e": 420.43, "t": "And in 2022, the National Mental Health Act modernizes rights, services and integration"}, {"s": 420.43, "e": 422.76, "t": "of mental health into general care."}, {"s": 422.76, "e": 428.28, "t": "Set the two histories side by side and the picture becomes honest. While Boston was"}, {"s": 428.28, "e": 433.93, "t": "opening vocational bureaus and American armies were testing recruits, our context was"}, {"s": 433.93, "e": 439.71, "t": "running indigenous and faith-based helping, and a colonial school system with no formal"}, {"s": 439.71, "e": 445.43, "t": "guidance. While Division 17 professionalized and community mental health spread, newly"}, {"s": 445.43, "e": 451.28, "t": "independent Nigeria was building school guidance and university counselling units. While"}, {"s": 451.28, "e": 457.0, "t": "the global field turned multicultural and preventive, Nigeria was forming associations"}, {"s": 457.0, "e": 462.45, "t": "and opening graduate training in 1994. And while today's global field argues about"}, {"s": 462.45, "e": 467.9, "t": "evidence and teletherapy, Nigeria is consolidating regulation and research output."}, {"s": 467.9, "e": 473.62, "t": "Neither history is a footnote to the other; your practice lives at their intersection."}, {"s": 473.62, "e": 479.14, "t": "Beneath the history sit philosophical assumptions, and you should know yours. About"}, {"s": 479.14, "e": 484.8, "t": "persons: we assume people are more than their diagnoses; that they possess choice and"}, {"s": 484.8, "e": 490.59, "t": "agency, however constrained; that they carry a growth-oriented, self-righting tendency;"}, {"s": 490.59, "e": 496.05, "t": "and that mind, body, culture and spirit interlock, so holism is not a slogan but a"}, {"s": 496.05, "e": 501.44, "t": "method. About knowing and doing: we assume experience is best understood from the"}, {"s": 501.44, "e": 506.83, "t": "client's frame, which is phenomenology; that knowledge is provisional and must be"}, {"s": 506.83, "e": 512.28, "t": "tested, which is the scientist-practitioner; that culture constitutes distress and"}, {"s": 512.28, "e": 518.01, "t": "healing rather than decorating them; and that prevention, wherever possible, is kinder"}, {"s": 518.01, "e": 519.61, "t": "and cheaper than repair."}, {"s": 519.61, "e": 524.92, "t": "Name the six commitments and you can read any counseling text with X-ray vision."}, {"s": 524.92, "e": 530.51, "t": "Humanism: the person is worthier than the problem. Phenomenology: the client's lived"}, {"s": 530.51, "e": 536.09, "t": "experience is primary data. Developmentalism: behaviour makes sense against lifespan"}, {"s": 536.09, "e": 541.94, "t": "tasks. Contextualism: context, culture, class and gender shape every session. Prevention"}, {"s": 541.94, "e": 547.73, "t": "orientation: stop harm before it starts. Social justice: some distress is manufactured,"}, {"s": 547.73, "e": 553.58, "t": "and counselors answer it with advocacy as well as empathy. Every theory we meet in weeks"}, {"s": 553.58, "e": 557.24, "t": "four and five will be a different mixture of these six."}, {"s": 557.24, "e": 562.89, "t": "So what does history obligate you to do? Five things. Hold an identity: you inherit a"}, {"s": 562.89, "e": 568.68, "t": "tradition with values, not a bag of tricks. Hold humility: every idea, including yours,"}, {"s": 568.68, "e": 574.33, "t": "is dated and culturally located. Hold culture seriously: imported theories need local"}, {"s": 574.33, "e": 579.99, "t": "validation before you trust them with a client in Ibadan or Kano. Hold advocacy: this"}, {"s": 579.99, "e": 585.77, "t": "field grew whenever it answered a social need, and shrank whenever it did not. And hold"}, {"s": 585.77, "e": 591.63, "t": "the conversation open: your research questions continue a century-long argument; join it"}, {"s": 591.63, "e": 593.36, "t": "with evidence, not volume."}, {"s": 593.36, "e": 598.95, "t": "Gather the week. Counseling psychology grew from vocational guidance, psychometrics,"}, {"s": 598.95, "e": 604.27, "t": "mental hygiene and the person-centred revolution into a named specialty in 1946,"}, {"s": 604.27, "e": 609.86, "t": "professionalized through the scientist-practitioner model, and turned developmental,"}, {"s": 609.86, "e": 615.12, "t": "multicultural and preventive across the late century. Nigeria's story runs from"}, {"s": 615.12, "e": 620.71, "t": "indigenous and faith-based helping, through school guidance and university units, to"}, {"s": 620.71, "e": 626.3, "t": "graduate training at Nsukka in 1994, statutory registration, and the National Mental"}, {"s": 626.3, "e": 631.89, "t": "Health Act 2022. Underneath sit six philosophical commitments. History, in short, is"}, {"s": 631.89, "e": 633.62, "t": "your professional grammar."}, {"s": 633.62, "e": 639.14, "t": "Your task before week three. Build a ten-event timeline that interleaves global and"}, {"s": 639.14, "e": 644.74, "t": "Nigerian milestones, one sentence of significance per event; the interleaving is the"}, {"s": 644.74, "e": 650.13, "t": "point. Second, write one philosophical assumption you personally hold about human"}, {"s": 650.13, "e": 655.45, "t": "nature, then write how your counseling would change if it were false; bring both"}, {"s": 655.45, "e": 660.98, "t": "paragraphs to the seminar. Read the history chapters in Corey and Gladding, plus at"}, {"s": 660.98, "e": 666.57, "t": "least one scholarly account of counseling psychology's growth in Nigeria. Next week:"}, {"s": 666.57, "e": 672.36, "t": "where we sit among the helping professions, and the ethics of referral. See you in week"}, {"s": 672.36, "e": 672.76, "t": "three."}], "mode": "captions", "duration": 672.76}, {"id": "w03", "num": 3, "title": "Relationship to Other Disciplines and Helping Professions", "slides": [{"file": "/dist/slides/w03/01-title.png", "title": "Among the Helping Professions", "start": 0.0, "end": 31.1}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/02-outcomes.png", "title": "What you will be able to do by the end of this week", "start": 31.1, "end": 67.18}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/03-why-boundaries.png", "title": "Why professional boundaries matter", "start": 67.18, "end": 109.22}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/04-professions-table.png", "title": "Six helping professions at a glance", "start": 109.22, "end": 168.15}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/05-clinical-vs-counseling.png", "title": "Counseling psychology and clinical psychology", "start": 168.15, "end": 217.44}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/06-psychiatry.png", "title": "Psychiatry and the medical model", "start": 217.44, "end": 263.09}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/07-other-professions.png", "title": "Professions we work beside, not above", "start": 263.09, "end": 317.22}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/08-pastoral.png", "title": "Pastoral care: strengths, limits, collaboration", "start": 317.22, "end": 369.27}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/09-traditional-healers.png", "title": "Traditional healers: prevalence, reasons, ethics", "start": 369.27, "end": 426.01}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/10-referral-flow.png", "title": "The referral pathway in five moves", "start": 426.01, "end": 487.74}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/11-referral-ethics.png", "title": "The ethics of moving a client between worlds", "start": 487.74, "end": 536.2}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/12-teamwork.png", "title": "What we bring to the team, what we ask of it", "start": 536.2, "end": 580.76}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/13-no-health.png", "title": "no-health", "start": 580.76, "end": 617.42}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/14-identity-card.png", "title": "Your identity card: six distinctive contributions", "start": 617.42, "end": 661.66}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/15-summary.png", "title": "Week 3 in review", "start": 661.66, "end": 704.06}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/16-task.png", "title": "Applied task and next week", "start": 704.06, "end": 753.84}], "cues": [{"s": 0.0, "e": 0.92, "t": "Welcome to week three of CPY 701. Last week we saw where the field came from; this week"}, {"s": 0.92, "e": 0.84, "t": "we map where it sits. A profession is defined not only by what it does, but by what its"}, {"s": 0.84, "e": 0.63, "t": "neighbours do, and by what it refuses to do. By the end of this lecture you should be"}, {"s": 0.63, "e": 0.48, "t": "able to place counseling psychology confidently among clinical psychology, psychiatry,"}, {"s": 0.48, "e": 1.0, "t": "social work, nursing, pastoral care and traditional healing, and to move a client"}, {"s": 1.0, "e": 0.11, "t": "between those worlds ethically."}, {"s": 0.11, "e": 0.1, "t": "Four outcomes. One, contrast counseling psychology with clinical psychology, psychiatry,"}, {"s": 0.1, "e": 0.88, "t": "social work, nursing, pastoral care and traditional healing. Two, identify the unique"}, {"s": 0.88, "e": 0.8, "t": "contributions of our specialty to multidisciplinary work. Three, map a referral network"}, {"s": 0.8, "e": 0.66, "t": "for your own community, including the informal helping resources clients actually use."}, {"s": 0.66, "e": 0.3, "t": "Four, apply the ethics of referral: consent, warm handover, no abandonment, and the"}, {"s": 0.3, "e": 0.68, "t": "feedback loop. These are examination favourites, but more importantly, they are"}, {"s": 0.68, "e": 0.18, "t": "Monday-morning skills."}, {"s": 0.18, "e": 0.43, "t": "Why dwell on boundaries? Four reasons. Identity: you cannot offer what you cannot name;"}, {"s": 0.43, "e": 0.03, "t": "boundaries tell a client what they are actually buying when they sit with you."}, {"s": 0.03, "e": 0.77, "t": "Competence: our ethical codes bind practice to training, and crossing a boundary"}, {"s": 0.77, "e": 0.88, "t": "silently is how harm begins. Collaboration: clear roles make teamwork possible, while"}, {"s": 0.88, "e": 0.62, "t": "blurred roles turn a case conference into a turf war. And client safety: blurred"}, {"s": 0.62, "e": 0.87, "t": "boundaries produce duplication, contradiction and abandonment, three injuries no client"}, {"s": 0.87, "e": 0.83, "t": "deserves. Boundaries are not walls; they are the joints that let the helping system"}, {"s": 0.83, "e": 0.19, "t": "move."}, {"s": 0.19, "e": 0.51, "t": "Read the landscape row by row. Counseling psychology: postgraduate professional training"}, {"s": 0.51, "e": 0.47, "t": "with registration through the Counsellors Registration Council of Nigeria; focus on"}, {"s": 0.47, "e": 0.29, "t": "functioning, development and mild to moderate distress; methods of psychotherapy,"}, {"s": 0.29, "e": 0.96, "t": "assessment and prevention; no prescribing. Clinical psychology: doctorate-level"}, {"s": 0.96, "e": 0.07, "t": "training, heavier on severe psychopathology and test batteries. Psychiatry: a medical"}, {"s": 0.07, "e": 0.39, "t": "degree plus specialization; diagnosis and pharmacotherapy; the only row that prescribes."}, {"s": 0.39, "e": 0.06, "t": "Social work: welfare, protection and family systems through case management and"}, {"s": 0.06, "e": 0.38, "t": "advocacy. Psychiatric nursing: continuity of care, adherence and the therapeutic milieu."}, {"s": 0.38, "e": 0.7, "t": "Pastoral care: meaning, ritual and moral support under a faith community's mandate, with"}, {"s": 0.7, "e": 0.15, "t": "no state licence. Every row saves lives the other rows cannot."}, {"s": 0.15, "e": 0.85, "t": "Start with our nearest neighbour, clinical psychology. We share a scientific core and"}, {"s": 0.85, "e": 0.41, "t": "much training overlap, but the centres of gravity differ. Clinical psychology leans"}, {"s": 0.41, "e": 0.25, "t": "toward severe and chronic psychopathology, an assessment-heavy culture of batteries and"}, {"s": 0.25, "e": 0.61, "t": "differential diagnosis, hospital and forensic settings, and research on disorder"}, {"s": 0.61, "e": 0.11, "t": "mechanisms. Counseling psychology leans toward normative life challenges alongside"}, {"s": 0.11, "e": 0.81, "t": "disorder: study, work, love and loss; it treats strengths, functioning and vocational"}, {"s": 0.81, "e": 0.44, "t": "behaviour as first-class data; it lives in universities, communities, workplaces and"}, {"s": 0.44, "e": 0.21, "t": "private practice; and its research favourites are development, prevention, culture and"}, {"s": 0.21, "e": 0.43, "t": "the working alliance. Same family, different centre of gravity."}, {"s": 0.43, "e": 0.99, "t": "Now the medical interface. Psychiatry brings what we cannot: medical diagnosis, the"}, {"s": 0.99, "e": 0.83, "t": "exclusion of organic causes, pharmacotherapy, and risk management in severe illness. We"}, {"s": 0.83, "e": 0.73, "t": "interface through shared care: referral for medication review; counseling for adherence,"}, {"s": 0.73, "e": 0.63, "t": "for the distress of side effects, and for adjustment to a diagnosis; and psychoeducation"}, {"s": 0.63, "e": 0.53, "t": "for families carrying the illness home. Keep this attitude: medicine is not the enemy of"}, {"s": 0.53, "e": 0.09, "t": "talk, and medication is not the enemy of meaning; many clients need both, sequenced"}, {"s": 0.09, "e": 0.53, "t": "well. And avoid the classic error: counseling a client whose untreated medical or"}, {"s": 0.53, "e": 0.09, "t": "psychotic condition makes counseling unsafe or futile. Screen first, then sit down."}, {"s": 0.09, "e": 0.33, "t": "Beyond the clinic sit the professions we work beside, not above. Social work holds the"}, {"s": 0.33, "e": 0.43, "t": "system around the client: case management, welfare, housing, protection. Psychiatric"}, {"s": 0.43, "e": 0.81, "t": "nursing holds continuity: observation, adherence, the therapeutic milieu, day after day."}, {"s": 0.81, "e": 0.98, "t": "School guidance holds the developmental line: guidance curricula, career information,"}, {"s": 0.98, "e": 0.01, "t": "early identification. Rehabilitation services hold the return to work and community"}, {"s": 0.01, "e": 0.67, "t": "roles. Pastoral care holds meaning and ritual inside communities of faith. And"}, {"s": 0.67, "e": 0.69, "t": "traditional healing holds culturally congruent explanation and ritual, and for many"}, {"s": 0.69, "e": 0.93, "t": "clients it is the first door, not the last. A counselor who dismisses any of these six"}, {"s": 0.93, "e": 0.23, "t": "will lose clients to them; a counselor who understands them gains allies."}, {"s": 0.23, "e": 0.26, "t": "Consider pastoral care with particular care, because in our context it is often the"}, {"s": 0.26, "e": 0.35, "t": "first resort. Its strengths are trust and access: the pulpit is frequently the first"}, {"s": 0.35, "e": 0.52, "t": "clinic, speaking a language of meaning and hope, with continuity across the lifespan."}, {"s": 0.52, "e": 0.62, "t": "Its limits are real: confidentiality norms differ; some practices delay care or load"}, {"s": 0.62, "e": 0.06, "t": "guilt onto the sufferer; and training in psychopathology varies widely. The"}, {"s": 0.06, "e": 0.09, "t": "collaboration models that work are humble ones: consultation and respectful two-way"}, {"s": 0.09, "e": 0.11, "t": "referral, joint psychoeducation programmes, and mental-health literacy training for"}, {"s": 0.11, "e": 0.28, "t": "clergy who want it. Remember the client's reality: many clients want both a counselor"}, {"s": 0.28, "e": 0.27, "t": "and a pastor. Our job is to coordinate, not to compete."}, {"s": 0.27, "e": 0.69, "t": "Traditional healers deserve the same seriousness. In many communities a majority of"}, {"s": 0.69, "e": 0.11, "t": "people with mental health concerns consult a traditional or faith healer first. The"}, {"s": 0.11, "e": 0.46, "t": "reasons are rational: cultural congruence, cost, proximity, family acceptance, and"}, {"s": 0.46, "e": 0.01, "t": "explanations that make sense of suffering in the community's own idiom. The risks are"}, {"s": 0.01, "e": 0.11, "t": "equally real: delayed evidence-based care, occasionally harmful practices, and"}, {"s": 0.11, "e": 0.26, "t": "explanatory models that can override the client's own voice. Ethical engagement"}, {"s": 0.26, "e": 0.62, "t": "therefore looks like this: respect the worldview; ask openly what has already been"}, {"s": 0.62, "e": 0.78, "t": "tried; negotiate a plural pathway with the client's consent; and build referral"}, {"s": 0.78, "e": 0.39, "t": "relationships with community resources before a crisis forces improvisation. The World"}, {"s": 0.39, "e": 0.35, "t": "Health Organization's mental health gap action programme explicitly supports"}, {"s": 0.35, "e": 0.01, "t": "task-sharing and collaboration with community resources."}, {"s": 0.01, "e": 0.71, "t": "Turn the landscape into practice architecture: the referral pathway in five moves. One,"}, {"s": 0.71, "e": 0.11, "t": "screen: intake covers the presenting problem, risk, medical flags, and the client's"}, {"s": 0.11, "e": 0.58, "t": "help-seeking path so far, including healers and pastors already involved. Two, check"}, {"s": 0.58, "e": 0.37, "t": "competence: is this within my training, scope and current capacity? If doubtful, consult"}, {"s": 0.37, "e": 0.07, "t": "before proceeding. Three, route: in scope means a counseling plan; medical flags mean a"}, {"s": 0.07, "e": 0.47, "t": "physician first; severe or complex means shared care; social needs mean welfare and"}, {"s": 0.47, "e": 0.94, "t": "social work; spiritual needs mean a pastoral link with consent. Four, warm handover:"}, {"s": 0.94, "e": 0.65, "t": "introduce the client personally, transfer a concise summary, agree roles and consent in"}, {"s": 0.65, "e": 0.35, "t": "writing. Five, close the loop: follow up, request feedback, document. A referral is not"}, {"s": 0.35, "e": 0.74, "t": "complete until it is confirmed."}, {"s": 0.74, "e": 0.45, "t": "The ethics of moving a client between worlds reduce to five disciplines. Consent first:"}, {"s": 0.45, "e": 0.15, "t": "explain why, to whom, and exactly what information will travel, and record the client's"}, {"s": 0.15, "e": 0.47, "t": "decision. No abandonment: you remain responsible until the receiving professional"}, {"s": 0.47, "e": 0.91, "t": "accepts the handover; a phone number on paper is not a referral. Minimum necessary:"}, {"s": 0.91, "e": 0.69, "t": "share what the next professional needs, not the whole file; confidentiality survives the"}, {"s": 0.69, "e": 0.93, "t": "referral. Know your map: be able to name your nearest psychiatrist, neurologist,"}, {"s": 0.93, "e": 0.38, "t": "shelter, welfare office and crisis line before you need them, because crisis is the"}, {"s": 0.38, "e": 0.15, "t": "worst time to do research. And task-sharing: in low-resource settings it is ethical only"}, {"s": 0.15, "e": 0.22, "t": "with training, protocols and supervision, never as a shortcut."}, {"s": 0.22, "e": 0.73, "t": "Inside a multidisciplinary team, know your contribution and your conditions. What we"}, {"s": 0.73, "e": 0.58, "t": "bring: strengths-based functional assessment; brief, focal, evidence-based"}, {"s": 0.58, "e": 0.35, "t": "interventions; prevention and psychoeducation programme design; family work; and routine"}, {"s": 0.35, "e": 0.8, "t": "outcome measurement that tells the team whether help is helping. What we ask of the"}, {"s": 0.8, "e": 0.11, "t": "team: clear role boundaries and named responsibilities; consent-based information"}, {"s": 0.11, "e": 0.43, "t": "sharing rather than casual corridor disclosure; respectful case conferences where"}, {"s": 0.43, "e": 0.2, "t": "disagreement is allowed; joint review of shared clients; and protected counseling space,"}, {"s": 0.2, "e": 0.84, "t": "because a client who cannot speak privately will not speak truthfully. Bring, and ask,"}, {"s": 0.84, "e": 0.76, "t": "in that order."}, {"s": 0.76, "e": 0.95, "t": "One line to carry from this week: there is no health without mental health. That slogan,"}, {"s": 0.95, "e": 0.93, "t": "popularised in global policy discourse from 2007, is why mental health now belongs in"}, {"s": 0.93, "e": 0.77, "t": "primary care, in schools, in workplaces and in community programmes. It is also why"}, {"s": 0.77, "e": 0.75, "t": "counseling psychology is an integration profession: we translate between medicine and"}, {"s": 0.75, "e": 0.66, "t": "the person, between the community and the clinic, between what a client believes and"}, {"s": 0.66, "e": 0.64, "t": "what a client needs. Wherever health is being delivered, our competence has a seat at"}, {"s": 0.64, "e": 0.41, "t": "that table."}, {"s": 0.41, "e": 0.46, "t": "So carry an identity card with six entries. Strengths and development: functioning and"}, {"s": 0.46, "e": 0.3, "t": "growth, not only symptom counts. Brief focal intervention: evidence-based help that"}, {"s": 0.3, "e": 0.14, "t": "respects a client's time and money. Vocational expertise: career and work as mental"}, {"s": 0.14, "e": 0.26, "t": "health variables, our historical signature since Parsons. Prevention design: programmes"}, {"s": 0.26, "e": 0.45, "t": "that stop harm before it starts. Multicultural competence: culture treated as a clinical"}, {"s": 0.45, "e": 0.64, "t": "fact, including our own. And outcome measurement: we measure whether help helped, and we"}, {"s": 0.64, "e": 0.83, "t": "are willing to publish the answer. When a team forgets these contributions, remind them,"}, {"s": 0.83, "e": 0.66, "t": "with evidence, not volume."}, {"s": 0.66, "e": 0.04, "t": "Gather the week. Counseling psychology sits among six helping worlds, defined by"}, {"s": 0.04, "e": 0.63, "t": "emphasis: functioning, development, prevention and culture. Clinical psychology and"}, {"s": 0.63, "e": 0.28, "t": "psychiatry differ from us in centre of gravity and prescribing rights, not in worth."}, {"s": 0.28, "e": 0.13, "t": "Social work, nursing, school guidance, pastoral care and traditional healing are allies"}, {"s": 0.13, "e": 0.05, "t": "with distinct mandates, and our clients often use several of them at once. Referral is a"}, {"s": 0.05, "e": 0.57, "t": "five-move discipline: screen, check, route, warm handover, close the loop. And the"}, {"s": 0.57, "e": 0.22, "t": "ethics hold throughout: consent, no abandonment, minimum necessary disclosure, and a"}, {"s": 0.22, "e": 0.05, "t": "community map you built before the crisis."}, {"s": 0.05, "e": 0.84, "t": "Your task before week four has three parts. First, draw the referral map of your local"}, {"s": 0.84, "e": 0.22, "t": "government area: at least one named resource in each of six categories, medical,"}, {"s": 0.22, "e": 0.47, "t": "psychiatric, social, educational, faith-based and traditional. Second, write a"}, {"s": 0.47, "e": 0.04, "t": "one-hundred-and-fifty-word warm referral letter for this vignette: a"}, {"s": 0.04, "e": 0.9, "t": "twenty-nine-year-old teacher with low mood, weight loss and a morning-worse rhythm, who"}, {"s": 0.9, "e": 0.82, "t": "is currently seeing a traditional healer. Third, interview or telephone one professional"}, {"s": 0.82, "e": 0.54, "t": "from a neighbouring profession and ask a single question: what do you wish counselors"}, {"s": 0.54, "e": 0.05, "t": "understood about your work? Bring the answer to the seminar. Next week we open the"}, {"s": 0.05, "e": 0.84, "t": "theories: psychodynamic, humanistic and existential foundations. See you in week four."}], "mode": "narrated", "duration": 753.84, "video": "/dist/CPY701-W03-lecture.mp4", "vtt": "/dist/w03-captions.vtt"}]};
